            "review_title": "Review at Lupin Bistrot Et Vins",
            "review_text": "Marie Christine O\nFrance7 contributions\n0\nUninteresting\nAug 2026 • Friends\nMy opinion: An address that, in my opinion, does not quite deserve the prices charged.\nThe setting is pleasant, but I did not find the experience particularly remarkable. The cuisine remains quite simple indeed, a roast chicken with potatoes, for example, however correctly executed it may be, does not constitute for me a gastronomic experience that justifies such high prices!!!\nSame observation for the wines: the selection is interesting and rather serious, but some bottles are offered at prices that I find frankly high considering their cost and their positioning in France.\nIn summary, nothing bad, but a value for money that seemed very disappointing to me. At these prices, I expect more creativity, refinement, and above all, an experience that truly justifies the bill.\nI do not recommend this \"bistro\" restaurant\n\nMy Review\nIn my opinion, this is an address that doesn’t quite live up to its prices.\nThe setting is pleasant, but I didn’t find the overall experience particularly remarkable. The food is fairly simple: a roast chicken with potatoes, for example, may be well executed, but for me, this doesn’t constitute a dining experience that justifies such high prices.\nI felt the same about the wine selection: it is interesting and fairly well curated, but some bottles are offered at prices that I find genuinely high considering their price and positioning in France.\nOverall, there was nothing particularly bad, but I found the value for money disappointing. At these prices, I expect more creativity, refinement, and above all, an experience that truly justifies the bill.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nTranslated from French\nShow original\nWritten August 15, 2026",
            "rating": 5.0,
