            "review_title": "Review at Lupin Bistrot Et Vins",
            "review_text": "Claude G\nTaverny, France665 contributions\n0\nDiscovery of a Nugget in Thao Dien\nMay 2025 • Family\nWe love the Thao Dien area in the D2 and come there every time we stay. Nothing to do with the center of Saigon; in its little streets it seems that time has stood still, as in Le Lupin, Parisian bistro with its room all height and length and its 2 rows of bistro tables and chairs, benches against the wall, reproductions of old advertisements. In this village atmosphere the European boss warmly welcomes us with a few words in French.\nThe menu is relatively small which for us is a guarantee of quality and freshness of the products very well worked and presented. The bread is homemade.\n The server is discreet, smiling, efficient.\nI feasted with the duck confit and delight with the rum baba of the French Antilles generously watered.\nIf this bistro was only open in the evening, its bosses are right to open it also for lunch because I have seen that it is frequented by tourists but also regulars; we will return there.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nTranslated from French\nShow original\nWritten May 16, 2025",
