            "review_title": "Review at Lupin Bistrot Et Vins",
            "review_text": "Fred K\nPARIS380 contributions\n0\nIt's hard to tell if I enjoyed it or not\nJan 2025 • Business\nFrench restaurant in the expat district of the city. We had dinner with 3. The dishes arrived in scattered mode because we did not specify that we wanted everything at once, even if it seemed logical as we were 3 for 3 items ordered. The charcuterie board was correct, the seashell pot very good. The sole was visibly withered, probably waiting in the kitchen. On the wine side, we took a \"nature\" wine that looked nothing like a traditional nature wine, it was more a test made by a traditional producer. The bread wasn't crazy. The service was very good and the setting is nice and clean. For 3 courses and 1 bottle of wine, we paid 132€, which is very expensive compared to the standard of living of the country and even in France we probably would not have paid as much. That said, we see a business or relatively affluent clientele.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nTranslated from French\nShow original\nWritten January 20, 2025",
